1
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:11,180
Hi, this is Creator Office.

2
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,840
It’s a workflow for creating a script and turning
it into a finished video.

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,920
This Thai short is one example.

4
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:28,310
Once the script is ready, narration and scene
planning can run at the same time.

5
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:33,175
Some jobs need to continue an existing Codex
session.

6
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:38,475
I queue those requests, so they run in order

7
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:41,810
and other sessions can keep working.

8
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:45,850
This is the short open in the app.

9
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:50,470
I can play the narration while looking at the
artwork

10
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:53,550
and reading the Thai subtitles.

11
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:59,710
It’s where I check how everything fits together
before I render.

12
00:01:00,877 --> 00:01:05,157
These are two versions of the artwork for scene
two.

13
00:01:06,117 --> 00:01:11,437
The app kept the original on the left when it
saved the repair.

14
00:01:11,717 --> 00:01:16,917
On the right, you can see the seat and speech
bubble from the opening shot.

15
00:01:17,697 --> 00:01:22,197
Those details make the two images feel like they
belong in the same room.

16
00:01:22,917 --> 00:01:26,797
You’ll see the repaired version in the finished
video.

17
00:01:37,137 --> 00:01:39,357
That was the finished video.

18
00:01:39,637 --> 00:01:45,397
The images on screen now are frames I pulled from
the exported video.

19
00:01:45,837 --> 00:01:50,847
They show the repaired artwork alongside the Thai
subtitle.

20
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:56,527
I compared the full export with the timing saved
in the app.

21
00:01:56,947 --> 00:01:59,627
All subtitles kept the original text.

22
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:17,407
Then I’d watch the final video before deciding
whether to adjust it or not.

23
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:24,300
If you’d like to see more of the shorts I’ve made
with Creator Office,

24
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:30,560
I’ve linked Bear Knows It on YouTube and
Instagram below.

25
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,220
Thank you for watching.
